6	// to set once, separately, before any accessor ran — a step a refactor could silently drop (that
7	// exact regression shipped once; see the app's `tests/unit/lib-console-composition.test.ts`). Now
8	// the app builds one runtime with one call and every accessor closes over `deps` directly: there is
9	// no separate step left to forget.
10	//
11	// CALL THIS EXACTLY ONCE PER APP, AT MODULE SCOPE. Each accessor below (apart from
12	// `iamClientsForToken` and `iamClientsForAction`, see their own comments) is a React `cache()`
13	// wrapper, and `cache()` memoizes by the WRAPPER's identity, not by its arguments. A second
14	// `createConsoleRuntime()` call therefore makes a second, independent memoization identity for the
15	// same request: every accessor built from it runs its live call again — a second `Introspect`, a
16	// second `ListRoleGrants` walk (up to 50 tenancy reads), a second discovery probe. Outside a React
17	// server render `cache()` is a pass-through (measured on react 19.2.8), so no vitest tier can
18	// observe two calls behaving differently from one — only an e2e `Introspect` count can (PR 3).
